1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
 Hi! My name is Johanna and today I will talk about my mother tongue, which is Swedish!

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:19,000
 Yes! Swedish is a Northern Germanic language, which is closely related to Danish, Norwegian and Icelandic to some extent.

3
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:31,000
 This is because all of the languages here originate from the Nordic language, which was a language that was spoken in the Nordic countries over a thousand years ago.

4
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:39,000
 We have also received a lot of influences from both English and German, as well as French and Latin.

5
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:48,000
 And as more and more immigrants are coming to Sweden now during the last century, we have also received many loanwords from Arabic, Turkish, Serbian,

6
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,000
 Finnish, to name a few.

7
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:59,000
 Swedish is a wonderful language to know, I think. We have nice tonalities.

8
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:08,000
 I often hear from people who do not speak Swedish that it sounds like I am singing when I speak.

9
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:15,000
 And there are also many wonderful sounds in Swedish. A favorite word that I have is lake.

10
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:17,000
 Lake, listen to it.

11
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:18,000
 Lake.

12
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:23,000
 Nice. It's a nice sound, I think.

13
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:34,000
 There is a nice tongue twister that is basically impossible to learn if you do not have Swedish as a mother tongue, which has to do with lakes and nice things.

14
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,000
 And it goes like this.

15
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:42,000
 Seven seasick sailors were taken care of by seven nice nurses on a sinking ship in Shanghai.

16
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:44,000
 Claudia Omnikam.

17
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:47,000
 The tone is important in Swedish.

18
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:50,000
 It is important to know the meaning of a word.

19
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,000
 You will get an example.

20
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:53,000
 It is...

21
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:55,000
 Do you see the spirit?

22
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:56,000
 Or...

23
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,000
 Do you see the spirit?

24
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:01,000
 You may have heard the difference, maybe not.

25
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:03,000
 But there were two different words.

26
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:06,000
 Spirit and spirit.

27
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:12,000
 The first means spirit, which is a spiritual thing.

28
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:13,000
 And...

29
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,000
 A...

30
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:20,000
 The spirit is the definite form of a spirit, a bird.

31
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:27,000
 Warm greetings from Stockholm, even though it is winter and snow here.

32
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:29,000
 Take care, bye!

